<BaseLayout title="Privacy | Archytum" description="How Archytum handles website inquiries and visitor information.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="Collect less. Use it for the reason requested." lede="This notice describes the initial Archytum website. It must receive professional review before public launch." />
  <article class="content">
    <div class="notice"><strong>Draft for review.</strong> This page is implementation-ready copy, not legal advice.</div>
    <h2>Information collected</h2>
    <p>Archytum may collect the information you submit through the inquiry form, including your name, business email, organization, website, role, stated need, timeline, budget range, referral source, and consent choice. Microsoft Bookings may collect scheduling information when you choose to book an eligible meeting.</p>
    <h2>How information is used</h2>
    <p>Information is used to evaluate and respond to inquiries, schedule conversations, maintain a minimal sales pipeline, prevent abuse, and improve the clarity of Archytum’s services. A submission is not used to make an automatic eligibility or purchasing decision.</p>
    <h2>Service providers</h2>
    <p>The initial site uses GitHub Pages for hosting, Formspree for form delivery, and Microsoft 365 for email and scheduling. These providers process information under their own terms and privacy practices.</p>
    <h2>Tracking</h2>
    <p>The initial website does not intentionally use advertising pixels, behavioral profiling, session recording, or nonessential analytics cookies.</p>
    <h2>Retention and sharing</h2>
    <p>Archytum retains inquiry information only as long as it is operationally or legally needed. Information is not sold. It may be shared with service providers necessary to operate the inquiry process or when required by law.</p>
    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>You may ask Archytum to correct or delete inquiry information, subject to legal and operational requirements. Contact <a href="mailto:blake@archytum.com">blake@archytum.com</a>.</p>
    <h2>Do not submit sensitive data</h2>
    <p>Do not send passwords, authentication codes, payment credentials, Social Security numbers, health information, regulated data, confidential customer material, or production secrets through the website or ordinary email.</p>
    <p class="article-meta">Last updated: September 28, 2026</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
